coefficient table `T_0 .. T_162` (its recursion is checked once on these literals, because the kernel
evaluates `chebSum` lazily and exponentially); the strict-exponent Horner `horn2` and the cell checkers
`rowTerm1`, `colTerm1` built on it, with equalities to the checkers `rowTerm`, `colTerm` of `AnchorE2`
(`horn2` carries the exponent instead of recomputing `q.length` at every step: 125 -> 66 ms per `FSq`); the
integer polynomials `zRof`, `zCof` of the two frozen K = 160 signed families (design C, TrialC) as literals; and the chain
lemmas that the slice modules and the assembly use.
